    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d863">

                <pb facs="0965" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg955"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1161 Johnston, Eric/1: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-25T23:00:00+03:00">March 25, 1944—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 26—1:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1044. Have learned from press that Eric Johnston<anchor n="43" xml:id="d863-f1"/>
                    is planning to come to Russia middle of May. Would appreciate advice on the
                    details of the purposes of his trip and the Department’s views. I welcome his
                    trip and believe his objective should be to obtain information <pb facs="0966"
                        n="956" xml:id="pg956"/> and create goodwill. I hope Mr. Johnston will be
                    asked to discuss postwar trade matters only in the most general way and after
                    consultation with me.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d863-f1" n="43" xml:id="d863-f1-content">
                <p>Eric A. Johnston, President of the United States Chamber of Commerce.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
